Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.42,0:00:21.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎收看《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:00:20.42,0:00:21.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Today on how it's made.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.96,0:00:27.82,Translation,,0,0,0,,全息照片，面向未来的投影技术
Dialogue: 1,0:00:24.96,0:00:27.82,Original,,0,0,0,,Holograms, projections for the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.16,0:00:33.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,包装印刷，属于大众的安迪·沃霍尔
Dialogue: 1,0:00:30.16,0:00:33.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Package printing, Andy Warhol for the masses.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:30.16,0:00:33.91,Annotation,,0,0,0,,安迪·沃霍尔，波普艺术代表画家
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.70,0:00:39.54,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮肤培植，重度烧伤者的希望
Dialogue: 1,0:00:35.70,0:00:39.54,Original,,0,0,0,,Skin culture, hope for those who suffered severe burns.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.60,0:00:46.98,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有罐装甜玉米，从玉米棒到罐头只需几把快刀
Dialogue: 1,0:00:41.60,0:00:46.98,Original,,0,0,0,,And canned sweetcorn, from top to can via a few sharp knives.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.28,0:00:52.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,但首先，全息照片不只是美丽迷人
Dialogue: 1,0:00:47.28,0:00:52.08,Original,,0,0,0,,But first, holograms aren't just beautiful and fascinating.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.48,0:00:55.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,它们自带一种高科技的神秘感
Dialogue: 1,0:00:52.48,0:00:55.12,Original,,0,0,0,,They have a certain high-tech mystique about them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.84,0:00:58.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,那么，是时候揭开谜底了
Dialogue: 1,0:00:55.84,0:00:58.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Well, it's high time we reveal the mystery.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.96,0:01:02.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,全息照片其实就是图像的层叠变化
Dialogue: 1,0:00:58.96,0:01:02.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Holograms are simply layered variations of an image,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.04,0:01:06.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,每一层都以不同的方式反射光线
Dialogue: 1,0:01:03.04,0:01:06.56,Original,,0,0,0,,each one causing light to reflect in a different way.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.48,0:01:18.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,全息照片是一种由两束激光的干涉产生的三维照片 
Dialogue: 1,0:01:12.48,0:01:18.80,Original,,0,0,0,,A hologram is a three-dimensional photograph produced by the interference of two laser beams.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.00,0:01:23.38,Translation,,0,0,0,,光线的颜色随波长不同而变化
Dialogue: 1,0:01:20.00,0:01:23.38,Original,,0,0,0,,The colour of light rays varies according to the wavelength.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.48,0:01:29.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,快门开启时，要么挡住光线，要么让光线通过
Dialogue: 1,0:01:24.48,0:01:29.76,Original,,0,0,0,,A shutter, when activated, either blocks or lets the light ray pass through.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.44,0:01:34.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里，光束以90度角一分为二
Dialogue: 1,0:01:31.44,0:01:34.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Here, the beam is split in two at a 90° angle.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.72,0:01:40.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,屏幕上清晰可见两束光的干涉
Dialogue: 1,0:01:36.72,0:01:40.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The interference of the two beams is clearly visible on the screen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.68,0:01:43.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,干涉条纹非常清晰分明
Dialogue: 1,0:01:41.68,0:01:43.84,Original,,0,0,0,,It has highly defined fringes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.88,0:01:46.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,光束需要保持稳定
Dialogue: 1,0:01:44.88,0:01:46.68,Original,,0,0,0,,The beams need stability
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.68,0:01:52.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,因为投射在屏幕上的干涉图案对微小振动极其敏感
Dialogue: 1,0:01:46.68,0:01:52.64,Original,,0,0,0,,because the pattern of interference projected on the screen is extremely sensitive to minute vibrations.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.84,0:01:56.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,轻轻敲一下桌子就可能毁掉它
Dialogue: 1,0:01:53.84,0:01:56.56,Original,,0,0,0,,A light tap on the table can easily spoil it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.80,0:02:03.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,团队将用这个黏土雕塑制作全息照片
Dialogue: 1,0:01:58.80,0:02:03.20,Original,,0,0,0,,The team will create a hologram from this sculpture made of modelling clay.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.08,0:02:10.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,雕塑用磁性底座固定，确保纹丝不动
Dialogue: 1,0:02:06.08,0:02:10.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The sculpture is positioned with a magnetic base for tremor-free support.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.68,0:02:13.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后在物体前方放置一块玻璃
Dialogue: 1,0:02:11.68,0:02:13.92,Original,,0,0,0,,They then place a glass in front of the object.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.08,0:02:20.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里就是光束经过的准确位置
Dialogue: 1,0:02:18.08,0:02:20.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Here's the exact point where the light beam passes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.36,0:02:29.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,为达到绝对稳定，工作台是一块2吨重的钢板，由18个气垫支撑
Dialogue: 1,0:02:23.36,0:02:29.84,Original,,0,0,0,,To achieve absolute stability, the table is a 2-ton block of steel which rests on 18 air tubes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.20,0:02:41.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,分束器将光束一分为二
Dialogue: 1,0:02:39.20,0:02:41.68,Original,,0,0,0,,A beam splitter separates the beam in two,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.24,0:02:45.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,一束射向物体后方，另一束射向前方
Dialogue: 1,0:02:42.24,0:02:45.52,Original,,0,0,0,,directing one behind the object and the other in front of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.88,0:02:50.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,其中一束光射向雕塑前方
Dialogue: 1,0:02:46.88,0:02:50.00,Original,,0,0,0,,One part of the beam heads toward the front of the sculpture.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.80,0:02:55.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,光束先经过物镜，使光线扩散
Dialogue: 1,0:02:50.80,0:02:55.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The beam first passes through an objective lens, which diffuses the light.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.32,0:02:58.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后被抛物面镜反射
Dialogue: 1,0:02:56.32,0:02:58.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Then it's reflected by a parabolic mirror,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.88,0:03:01.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,以免光强损失过多
Dialogue: 1,0:02:58.88,0:03:01.68,Original,,0,0,0,,which prevents it from losing too much of its intensity.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.40,0:03:04.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,和摄影一样，这里也需要胶片
Dialogue: 1,0:03:02.40,0:03:04.64,Original,,0,0,0,,As in photography, film is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.44,0:03:08.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,全息胶片附着在一块玻璃板上
Dialogue: 1,0:03:05.44,0:03:08.40,Original,,0,0,0,,This holographic film is attached to a glass plate.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.80,0:03:14.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,再盖上一块玻璃板，把胶片固定住
Dialogue: 1,0:03:10.80,0:03:14.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Then another glass plate is added so that the film is secure.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.96,0:03:19.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,任何大于激光波长1/10的位移都会毁掉图像
Dialogue: 1,0:03:14.96,0:03:19.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Any movement greater than 1/10 of the laser's wavelength will spoil the image.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.60,0:03:29.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在打开激光器
Dialogue: 1,0:03:27.60,0:03:29.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The laser is now turned on.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.32,0:03:34.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,光强达到约250毫瓦
Dialogue: 1,0:03:30.32,0:03:34.48,Original,,0,0,0,,The intensity of light ray reaches about 250 milliwatts.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.40,0:03:40.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,模型正常曝光时间约为1秒
Dialogue: 1,0:03:36.40,0:03:40.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The normal exposure time of the model to the beam is about 1 second.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.96,0:03:46.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,但用脉冲激光制作的全息照片，曝光时间极短
Dialogue: 1,0:03:42.96,0:03:46.88,Original,,0,0,0,,But some holograms made with a pulsed laser are exposed
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.96,0:03:51.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,仅有12纳秒，比普通曝光短得多
Dialogue: 1,0:03:46.96,0:03:51.60,Original,,0,0,0,,to the light for 12 nanoseconds, an infinitely shorter period of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.28,0:04:12.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,和摄影一样，胶片需要显影
Dialogue: 1,0:04:09.28,0:04:12.08,Original,,0,0,0,,As in photography, the film has to be developed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.04,0:04:16.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些盘子里装着化学溶液，称为显影液
Dialogue: 1,0:04:13.04,0:04:16.48,Original,,0,0,0,,These trays contain chemical solutions, called developer.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.68,0:04:20.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,首先，胶片在显影液中浸泡2分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:04:17.68,0:04:20.80,Original,,0,0,0,,First, the film is soaked in the developer for 2 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.52,0:04:25.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这种溶液会使感光的银盐变黑
Dialogue: 1,0:04:21.52,0:04:25.60,Original,,0,0,0,,This solution blackens the silver salts, which have reacted to the light.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.24,0:04:32.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后胶片浸泡在漂白液中，彻底清除变黑的银盐
Dialogue: 1,0:04:26.24,0:04:32.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the film is soaked in a solution called bleach to completely eliminate the silver salts which blackened it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.40,0:04:37.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在冲洗胶片
Dialogue: 1,0:04:36.40,0:04:37.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the film is rinsed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.56,0:04:44.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,这一步用于去除感光乳剂中的酸性物质，以免污染下一道溶液
Dialogue: 1,0:04:38.56,0:04:44.40,Original,,0,0,0,,This step is used to eliminate the acids in the emulsion, so as not to contaminate the next solution.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.60,0:04:52.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,胶片慢慢变得透明
Dialogue: 1,0:04:49.60,0:04:52.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The film slowly becomes transparent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.36,0:05:00.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后用清水冲洗
Dialogue: 1,0:04:59.36,0:05:00.80,Original,,0,0,0,,It's then rinsed in clear water.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.68,0:05:06.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,再在润湿剂中浸泡1分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:05:03.68,0:05:06.24,Original,,0,0,0,,And it's soaked for 1 minute in a wetting agent,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.40,0:05:08.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,以消除所有水渍
Dialogue: 1,0:05:06.40,0:05:08.00,Original,,0,0,0,,which eliminates all water spots.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.96,0:05:13.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后胶片干燥，显现它的奥秘
Dialogue: 1,0:05:10.96,0:05:13.92,Original,,0,0,0,,The film is then dried to reveal its secrets.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.96,0:05:18.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,这就是从雕塑制作出的全息成品
Dialogue: 1,0:05:14.96,0:05:18.16,Original,,0,0,0,,And here's the finished hologram, created from the sculpture.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.80,0:05:27.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,有些全息照片可以动起来，由一系列静态全息图生成
Dialogue: 1,0:05:22.80,0:05:27.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Some holograms can be animated, which are generated from a series of still holograms.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.24,0:05:30.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,根据项目的复杂程度
Dialogue: 1,0:05:28.24,0:05:30.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Depending on the complexity of the project,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.72,0:05:34.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,制作一张全息照片需要1到5小时
Dialogue: 1,0:05:30.72,0:05:34.16,Original,,0,0,0,,a hologram can be produced in between 1 and 5 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.64,0:05:36.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,懂得原理后，其实很简单
Dialogue: 1,0:05:34.64,0:05:36.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Simple once you know how.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.84,0:05:47.82,Translation,,0,0,0,,普通的产品包装上塞满了各种信息
Dialogue: 1,0:05:43.84,0:05:47.82,Original,,0,0,0,,Your average product packaging is crammed with so much information
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.82,0:05:51.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,很难看出藏在说明和配料背后的艺术
Dialogue: 1,0:05:47.82,0:05:51.84,Original,,0,0,0,,it's hard to see the artistry behind the instructions and ingredients.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.96,0:05:55.94,Translation,,0,0,0,,制作包装需要投入大量心思
Dialogue: 1,0:05:52.96,0:05:55.94,Original,,0,0,0,,An incredible amount of thought goes into making packaging
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.94,0:06:00.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,让包装独一无二、过目难忘，并吸引消费者
Dialogue: 1,0:05:55.94,0:06:00.48,Original,,0,0,0,,that's unique, instantly recognisable, and attractive to the consumer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.24,0:06:09.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,所有消费品都或多或少有包装
Dialogue: 1,0:06:06.24,0:06:09.12,Original,,0,0,0,,All consumer products are packaged in one way or another.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.08,0:06:13.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,制作从烧蚀铝版开始
Dialogue: 1,0:06:10.08,0:06:13.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Fabrication starts with the burning of an aluminium plate.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.58,0:06:26.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,铝版装到滚筒上，用激光开始烧蚀
Dialogue: 1,0:06:21.58,0:06:26.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The plate is placed onto a cylinder, and using a laser, the burning begins.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.00,0:06:29.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,图像6分钟即可显现
Dialogue: 1,0:06:28.00,0:06:29.92,Original,,0,0,0,,The image appears in 6 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.36,0:06:34.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,这块印版将用来在包装上压印图案
Dialogue: 1,0:06:31.36,0:06:34.24,Original,,0,0,0,,This plate will make the printing impressions on packages.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.28,0:06:39.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,激光必须校准得十分精确
Dialogue: 1,0:06:37.28,0:06:39.68,Original,,0,0,0,,The laser has to be perfectly calibrated.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.00,0:06:41.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,用这块测试印版
Dialogue: 1,0:06:40.00,0:06:41.12,Original,,0,0,0,,Using this test plate,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.48,0:06:52.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,印刷从手工调配油墨开始
Dialogue: 1,0:06:50.48,0:06:52.88,Original,,0,0,0,,printing starts with the hand mixing of inks.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.72,0:06:56.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,如果没有现成想要的颜色
Dialogue: 1,0:06:54.72,0:06:56.72,Original,,0,0,0,,If the desired colour does not exist,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.04,0:06:59.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,就要用各种其他颜色调配出来
Dialogue: 1,0:06:57.04,0:06:59.52,Original,,0,0,0,,it has to be made up from a mix of various other colours.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.28,0:07:02.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,用刮刀进行油墨试印
Dialogue: 1,0:07:01.28,0:07:02.96,Original,,0,0,0,,An ink trial is done with a spatula,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.84,0:07:07.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,再用手动小压机进行颜色测试
Dialogue: 1,0:07:03.84,0:07:07.44,Original,,0,0,0,,and using this small manual press, colour ink tests are done.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.80,0:07:12.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,油墨涂在纸上，与原稿颜色对比
Dialogue: 1,0:07:08.80,0:07:12.96,Original,,0,0,0,,The ink is spread onto paper, and the colour compared to the master design.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.92,0:07:16.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,如果颜色一致，就可以开动印刷机
Dialogue: 1,0:07:13.92,0:07:16.48,Original,,0,0,0,,If they do match, the presses can be started up.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.60,0:07:20.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,这是六色胶印印刷机
Dialogue: 1,0:07:17.60,0:07:21.04,Original,,0,0,0,,This is a six colour offset process printing press.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.32,0:07:30.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,印刷机通过吸附和摩擦供纸，每小时吞吐8000张
Dialogue: 1,0:07:24.32,0:07:30.08,Original,,0,0,0,,The press is fed by a suction and friction process, devouring 8,000 sheets an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.52,0:07:34.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在把印版装到印刷机滚筒上
Dialogue: 1,0:07:31.52,0:07:34.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the printing plate is placed onto the press cylinder.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.12,0:07:37.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,这块印版将接触到着墨辊
Dialogue: 1,0:07:35.12,0:07:37.76,Original,,0,0,0,,This plate will come into contact with the inking rollers,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.76,0:07:39.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些辊筒从墨斗中取墨
Dialogue: 1,0:07:37.76,0:07:39.60,Original,,0,0,0,,which feed off the ink reservoir.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.30,0:07:44.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,为防止油墨干燥，振荡器会维持油墨粘度
Dialogue: 1,0:07:40.30,0:07:44.56,Original,,0,0,0,,To prevent it from drying, ink viscosity is maintained with an oscillator.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.36,0:07:50.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,印刷机启动，单小时产量达8000印
Dialogue: 1,0:07:45.36,0:07:50.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The press starts up and reaches a production rate of 8,000 impressions in a single hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.56,0:07:55.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,印刷机由多个独立颜色印刷单元组成
Dialogue: 1,0:07:52.56,0:07:55.68,Original,,0,0,0,,The press is comprised of individual colour printing units.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.88,0:07:59.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,纸张依次通过各个单元
Dialogue: 1,0:07:56.88,0:07:59.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The paper sheet passes from one unit to the other.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.00,0:08:01.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,每一步都印上一种新颜色
Dialogue: 1,0:08:00.00,0:08:01.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Receiving a new colour at each step.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.04,0:08:07.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,最终质检确保颜色和位置准确无误
Dialogue: 1,0:08:03.04,0:08:07.12,Original,,0,0,0,,A final quality check guarantees that the colours and position is correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.52,0:08:14.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后一步是纸盒的折叠与粘合
Dialogue: 1,0:08:11.52,0:08:14.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The final step is the folding and gluing of the boxes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.60,0:08:18.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,这块压痕板在纸板上压出折痕
Dialogue: 1,0:08:15.60,0:08:18.72,Original,,0,0,0,,This grooved plate makes folding marks on the carton.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.00,0:08:27.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器完成切割、压痕以及除废，每小时处理6000张
Dialogue: 1,0:08:20.00,0:08:27.04,Original,,0,0,0,,And this machine does the cutting, the embossing, and stripping of the sheets at a rate of 6,000 an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.96,0:08:31.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,模切刀切开纸板
Dialogue: 1,0:08:28.96,0:08:31.84,Original,,0,0,0,,The cutting die slices the carton sheets and,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.00,0:08:34.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,配合压痕板形成折边
Dialogue: 1,0:08:32.00,0:08:34.64,Original,,0,0,0,,together with the grooved plate, makes the folding joints.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.68,0:08:48.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,这块垫板滑入模切刀后方，使切割受力均匀
Dialogue: 1,0:08:43.68,0:08:48.16,Original,,0,0,0,,This sheet is slid behind the cutting die to equalise the cutting of the sheets.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.20,0:08:55.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,这堆积如山的3000张纸板即将开始切割
Dialogue: 1,0:08:51.20,0:08:55.04,Original,,0,0,0,,This enormous pile of 3,000 sheets is now ready to be cut.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.80,0:09:05.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,压痕机的进料装置每小时处理6000到8000张
Dialogue: 1,0:09:00.80,0:09:05.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The embossing press feeder handles between 6 and 8,000 sheets an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.32,0:09:08.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,辊轮引导纸板进入压痕机
Dialogue: 1,0:09:06.32,0:09:08.80,Original,,0,0,0,,Rollers guide the sheets in the direction of the press,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.16,0:09:14.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,纸板在这里被机器压出痕迹
Dialogue: 1,0:09:12.16,0:09:14.96,Original,,0,0,0,,and here the sheets are embossed by the machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.80,0:09:21.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后检验压痕的精度
Dialogue: 1,0:09:18.80,0:09:21.20,Original,,0,0,0,,The precision of the embossing is then verified.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.32,0:09:28.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来是纸板的模切
Dialogue: 1,0:09:26.32,0:09:28.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Next comes the cutting of the sheets.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.60,0:09:34.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,模切单元剥离去除多余部分
Dialogue: 1,0:09:31.60,0:09:34.72,Original,,0,0,0,,The cutting unit strips and removes the unnecessary
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.80,0:09:39.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,纸板碎片被吸走，最终送去回收
Dialogue: 1,0:09:34.80,0:09:39.36,Original,,0,0,0,,pieces, and the carton scraps are sucked up for eventual recycling.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.28,0:09:46.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,边角料也可以用手锤敲掉
Dialogue: 1,0:09:43.28,0:09:46.56,Original,,0,0,0,,The scraps can also be cut away manually using a hammer,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.80,0:09:52.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,纸板端头料送去回收
Dialogue: 1,0:09:48.80,0:09:52.00,Original,,0,0,0,,and the carton end pieces are sent off for recycling.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.28,0:09:59.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,剩下的就是纸盒组装
Dialogue: 1,0:09:57.28,0:09:59.84,Original,,0,0,0,,All that remains is the assembly of the packages.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.72,0:10:05.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,高速粘合机每小时能生产3万到4万个纸盒
Dialogue: 1,0:10:00.72,0:10:05.68,Original,,0,0,0,,With a high-speed gluing unit that can construct 30,000 to 40,000 boxes per hour,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.44,0:10:11.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,粘合从沿折痕折叠纸板开始
Dialogue: 1,0:10:07.44,0:10:11.52,Original,,0,0,0,,gluing begins with the folding of the sheets, following the folding marks.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.16,0:10:14.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,成型的纸盒侧面随后粘合在一起
Dialogue: 1,0:10:12.16,0:10:14.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The sides of the formed box are then glued together.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.00,0:10:20.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,制作一个包装盒平均需要5到8道工序
Dialogue: 1,0:10:16.00,0:10:20.48,Original,,0,0,0,,An average of between 5 to 8 steps are needed to fabricate a packaging box.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.68,0:10:26.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家工厂每天生产100万到200万个纸盒
Dialogue: 1,0:10:21.68,0:10:26.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Every day, this plant produces between 1 and 2 million boxes,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.88,0:10:31.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,每年需要近4000吨纸板
Dialogue: 1,0:10:26.88,0:10:31.04,Original,,0,0,0,,requiring almost 4,000 tons of cardboard every year.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.84,0:10:37.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来是《造物小百科》：皮肤培植
Dialogue: 1,0:10:33.84,0:10:37.12,Original,,0,0,0,,Coming up in how it's made: skin cultures,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.16,0:10:41.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮肤移植可以决定生死
Dialogue: 1,0:10:38.16,0:10:41.04,Original,,0,0,0,,skin grafts can mean the difference between life and death,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.76,0:10:44.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,为重度烧伤者带来希望
Dialogue: 1,0:10:41.76,0:10:44.08,Original,,0,0,0,,offering hope for those who've suffered severe burns.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.16,0:10:47.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有罐装甜玉米
Dialogue: 1,0:10:46.16,0:10:47.20,Original,,0,0,0,,And canned sweet corn.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.92,0:10:53.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,对工程壮举感兴趣的人都会欣赏从玉米棒到罐头的旋风之旅
Dialogue: 1,0:10:47.92,0:10:53.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Anyone with an appetite for feats of engineering will appreciate the whirlwind journey from cob to can.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.40,0:10:55.54,Translation,,0,0,0,,广告之后见
Dialogue: 1,0:10:54.40,0:10:55.54,Original,,0,0,0,,See you after the break.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.68,0:11:08.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎回到《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:11:05.68,0:11:08.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome back to how it's made.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.32,0:11:10.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,稍后我们将介绍罐装甜玉米
Dialogue: 1,0:11:08.32,0:11:10.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Later we look at canned sweet corn,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.04,0:11:13.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,一场从玉米棒到罐头的旋风工程
Dialogue: 1,0:11:11.04,0:11:13.60,Original,,0,0,0,,a feat of whirlwind engineering from cob to can.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.32,0:11:20.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,但首先，来看看重度烧伤患者
Dialogue: 1,0:11:16.32,0:11:20.00,Original,,0,0,0,,But first, for people who've suffered severe burns.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.46,0:11:21.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,他们不是绝望的
Dialogue: 1,0:11:20.46,0:11:21.64,Original,,0,0,0,,There's hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.72,0:11:24.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,可以用皮肤移植治疗
Dialogue: 1,0:11:22.72,0:11:24.80,Original,,0,0,0,,They can be treated with skin grafts,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.88,0:11:28.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,移植实验室培育的人类皮肤
Dialogue: 1,0:11:24.88,0:11:28.00,Original,,0,0,0,,using human skin that's been cultured in a lab.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.76,0:11:36.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,接受移植的患者，往往疤痕更少，愈合时间也短得多
Dialogue: 1,0:11:29.76,0:11:36.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Patients who receive these grafts tend to develop less scarring and usually heal in a fraction of the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.16,0:11:46.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,要培植皮肤，必须先分离、收集皮肤细胞并让其增殖
Dialogue: 1,0:11:41.16,0:11:46.44,Original,,0,0,0,,To grow skin, skin cells have to be isolated and collected and made to multiply.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.92,0:11:53.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,一切始于取一小块皮肤样本
Dialogue: 1,0:11:49.92,0:11:53.28,Original,,0,0,0,,It all begins with the removal of a small skin sample.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.24,0:11:57.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,这块样本中的1000万个细胞足以培养一份皮肤
Dialogue: 1,0:11:54.24,0:11:57.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The 10 million cells in this piece are enough to make a culture.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.80,0:12:00.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮肤浸泡其中
Dialogue: 1,0:11:58.80,0:12:00.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The skin soaks in.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.00,0:12:02.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,培养基中含有青霉素和庆大霉素
Dialogue: 1,0:12:00.00,0:12:02.80,Original,,0,0,0,,A medium containing penicillin and gentamycin,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.44,0:12:06.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,这两种抗生素可防止细菌感染
Dialogue: 1,0:12:03.44,0:12:06.40,Original,,0,0,0,,antibiotics which protect it from bacterial infection.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.12,0:12:12.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在取一小块皮肤，在培养皿上用手术刀精细切分
Dialogue: 1,0:12:07.12,0:12:12.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Now a piece of skin is cut and delicately sectioned on a petri dish with a scalpel.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.96,0:12:15.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,小心地把脂肪与真皮分离
Dialogue: 1,0:12:12.96,0:12:15.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The fat is gently detached from the dermis,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.00,0:12:17.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,因为培养用不到脂肪
Dialogue: 1,0:12:16.00,0:12:17.92,Original,,0,0,0,,since it will not be needed in the culturing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.88,0:12:22.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮肤切成细条，因为嗜热菌蛋白酶
Dialogue: 1,0:12:18.88,0:12:22.72,Original,,0,0,0,,The skin is cut into thin strips, because thermolysin,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.04,0:12:28.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,这种分离真皮与表皮的酶，在小面积上作用更高效
Dialogue: 1,0:12:23.04,0:12:28.88,Original,,0,0,0,,the enzyme which separates the dermis from the epidermis, acts more efficiently on small surfaces.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.76,0:12:34.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后一种酶破坏真皮与表皮细胞之间的联系
Dialogue: 1,0:12:29.76,0:12:34.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Then an enzyme destroys the links uniting the dermis and epidermis cells.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.64,0:12:41.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,该过程在37摄氏度培养箱中培养3小时
Dialogue: 1,0:12:35.64,0:12:41.88,Original,,0,0,0,,This procedure is carried out in this incubator over three hours at a temperature of 37 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.00,0:12:47.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,培养结束后，取出培养皿离开培养箱
Dialogue: 1,0:12:43.00,0:12:47.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Once incubation is over, the petri dish is removed from the incubator.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.68,0:12:54.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,只保留表皮细胞，即角质形成细胞
Dialogue: 1,0:12:50.68,0:12:54.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Only the epidermis cells, called keratinocytes, are retained.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.48,0:12:59.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,表皮与真皮被精确地分离开
Dialogue: 1,0:12:55.48,0:12:59.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The epidermis is detached from the dermis with great precision.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.44,0:13:05.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在把皮肤条放入胰蛋白酶处理单元
Dialogue: 1,0:13:02.44,0:13:05.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the strips are placed in a trypsination unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.20,0:13:11.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,一种酶会破坏表皮细胞间的连接，以便分离它们
Dialogue: 1,0:13:06.20,0:13:11.24,Original,,0,0,0,,An enzyme will destroy the links uniting the epidermis cells in order to isolate them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.92,0:13:15.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,这一操作促使细胞增殖
Dialogue: 1,0:13:12.92,0:13:15.88,Original,,0,0,0,,This operation signals the cells to multiply.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.32,0:13:23.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,为了提高胰蛋白酶的效力，处理单元被放在振荡器上
Dialogue: 1,0:13:17.32,0:13:23.08,Original,,0,0,0,,In order to increase the effectiveness of trypsin, the trypsination unit is placed on an agitator.
Dialogue: 2,0:13:17.32,0:13:20.32,Annotation,,0,0,0,,胰蛋白酶：分解蛋白质的酶
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.80,0:13:29.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,含细胞的悬浮液被抽出
Dialogue: 1,0:13:25.80,0:13:29.72,Original,,0,0,0,,The liquid containing the cells in suspension is drawn off.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.24,0:13:34.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在需要对液体进行分离
Dialogue: 1,0:13:33.24,0:13:34.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the liquid must be separated.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.04,0:13:45.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,所需的细胞位于试管底部，而上方的含胰蛋白酶上清液需要去除
Dialogue: 1,0:13:39.04,0:13:45.92,Original,,0,0,0,,The desired cells lie at the bottom of the tube, while the upper floating solution containing the trypsin has to be removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.24,0:13:53.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,用真空系统抽走胰蛋白酶溶液
Dialogue: 1,0:13:50.24,0:13:53.12,Original,,0,0,0,,The trypsin solution is drawn off with a vacuum system.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.00,0:14:02.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,为了清除所有胰蛋白酶残留
Dialogue: 1,0:14:00.00,0:14:02.20,Original,,0,0,0,,In order to eliminate all traces of trypsin,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.76,0:14:06.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,加入更多化学试剂，让混合物重新悬浮
Dialogue: 1,0:14:02.76,0:14:06.52,Original,,0,0,0,,further chemicals are added and the mixture put back into suspension.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.68,0:14:16.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在，小样本中的细胞需先计数，再进行第二次离心
Dialogue: 1,0:14:10.68,0:14:16.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the cells from the small skin sample have to be counted before being centrifuged a second time.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.28,0:14:23.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,细胞在显微镜下人工计数
Dialogue: 1,0:14:20.28,0:14:23.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The cells are counted by hand using a microscope.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.84,0:14:25.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,或用这种专用设备
Dialogue: 1,0:14:23.84,0:14:25.60,Original,,0,0,0,,or in this specialist equipment.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.40,0:14:30.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,确定活组织检查所得细胞的确切数量
Dialogue: 1,0:14:26.40,0:14:30.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The exact number of cells obtained during a biopsy is determined
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.42,0:14:33.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,并筛选最适合生长的皮肤细胞
Dialogue: 1,0:14:30.42,0:14:33.68,Original,,0,0,0,,as well as the best skin cells needed for maximum growth.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.04,0:14:46.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,角质形成细胞被分装到装有培养基的培养瓶中
Dialogue: 1,0:14:41.04,0:14:46.72,Original,,0,0,0,,The bottom portion of keratinocytes is divided in these flasks containing a culture medium,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.88,0:14:48.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,其成分与血液相似
Dialogue: 1,0:14:46.88,0:14:48.64,Original,,0,0,0,,whose composition resembles blood.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.72,0:14:58.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,放入37摄氏度的培养箱，细胞将在瓶中增殖一周
Dialogue: 1,0:14:52.72,0:14:58.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Placed in an oven at 37 degrees, the cells will multiply over a week in these flasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.44,0:15:03.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,浸泡细胞的溶液每2天更换一次
Dialogue: 1,0:14:59.44,0:15:03.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The solution in which the cells are immersed is changed every 2 days.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.20,0:15:13.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,不到一周，细胞几乎铺满整个培养瓶表面
Dialogue: 1,0:15:09.20,0:15:13.76,Original,,0,0,0,,In less than a week, the cells have almost covered the entire surface of the flask.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.76,0:15:19.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在可以再次用胰蛋白酶处理，扩增出50个新培养瓶
Dialogue: 1,0:15:15.76,0:15:19.84,Original,,0,0,0,,They can now be trypsinated anew to create a further 50 flasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.48,0:15:23.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些新瓶再放入培养箱约一周
Dialogue: 1,0:15:20.48,0:15:23.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Which in turn will be placed in the oven for about 1 week.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.92,0:15:34.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮肤片铺满培养瓶内壁
Dialogue: 1,0:15:31.92,0:15:34.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Skin strips carpet the inner surface of the flask.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.52,0:15:37.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后用刮刀将其剥离
Dialogue: 1,0:15:35.52,0:15:37.20,Original,,0,0,0,,They are then detached with a spatula.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.16,0:15:42.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,用类似烙铁的加热装置把培养瓶一分为二
Dialogue: 1,0:15:38.16,0:15:42.12,Original,,0,0,0,,The flasks are cut in two with a heating unit resembling a soldering iron.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.88,0:15:53.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,为便于操作，在厚度不足0.1毫米的皮肤片上盖上纱布
Dialogue: 1,0:15:46.88,0:15:53.76,Original,,0,0,0,,To make handling easier, gauze is placed on the skin strips whose thickness is less than one tenth of a millimeter.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.08,0:15:58.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,移植物最终覆盖在伤口上
Dialogue: 1,0:15:56.08,0:15:58.56,Original,,0,0,0,,The graft is then finally placed on the wound.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.44,0:16:02.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,10天后取下夹子和纱布
Dialogue: 1,0:15:59.44,0:16:02.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Clamps and the gauze will be removed after 10 days,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.04,0:16:05.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,患者开始愈合
Dialogue: 1,0:16:03.04,0:16:05.44,Original,,0,0,0,,and the patient begins the healing process.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.44,0:16:17.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,说到蔬菜，没有比新鲜玉米棒更好的了
Dialogue: 1,0:16:13.44,0:16:17.60,Original,,0,0,0,,When it comes to vegetables, there's nothing like fresh corn on the cob.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.56,0:16:24.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,但正如任何学生所说，罐装甜玉米才是大学食堂的主料
Dialogue: 1,0:16:18.56,0:16:24.48,Original,,0,0,0,,But as any student will tell you, canned sweet corn is the staple ingredient in any university kitchen.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.52,0:16:27.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,任何对工程壮举有胃口的人
Dialogue: 1,0:16:25.52,0:16:27.92,Original,,0,0,0,,And anyone with an appetite for feats of engineering
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.40,0:16:31.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,都会欣赏从玉米棒到罐头的旋风之旅
Dialogue: 1,0:16:28.40,0:16:31.68,Original,,0,0,0,,will appreciate the whirlwind journey from cob to can.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.64,0:16:44.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,纵观历史，食物的保存方式包括烟熏、冷冻、风干和腌制
Dialogue: 1,0:16:38.64,0:16:44.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Throughout history, food. Preserving has included smoking, freezing, drying, and salting.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.36,0:16:48.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,19世纪初，尼古拉·阿佩尔建厂
Dialogue: 1,0:16:45.36,0:16:48.96,Original,,0,0,0,,In the early 19th century, Nicolas Appert built a factory
Dialogue: 2,0:16:45.36,0:16:48.36,Annotation,,0,0,0,,阿佩尔：罐头保藏法发明者
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.04,0:16:52.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,用密封玻璃罐保存食物
Dialogue: 1,0:16:49.04,0:16:52.48,Original,,0,0,0,,to preserve foods in hermetically sealed glass jars,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.96,0:16:54.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,并煮沸杀菌
Dialogue: 1,0:16:52.96,0:16:54.88,Original,,0,0,0,,and to sterilise them by boiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.84,0:16:59.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,但玻璃易碎，于是在1810年
Dialogue: 1,0:16:55.84,0:16:59.12,Original,,0,0,0,,But glass was breakable, and so in 1810,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.44,0:17:02.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,一位名叫杜兰德的英国人发明了马口铁罐头
Dialogue: 1,0:16:59.44,0:17:02.64,Original,,0,0,0,,an Englishman named Durand invented the tin can,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.04,0:17:06.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,最初在美国独立战争中为军方使用
Dialogue: 1,0:17:03.04,0:17:06.80,Original,,0,0,0,,first used by the military in the American War of Independence.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.76,0:17:21.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,用于罐装的玉米在8月中旬到10月中旬之间收获
Dialogue: 1,0:17:16.76,0:17:21.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Corn destined for canning is harvested from mid August to mid October.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.44,0:17:26.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,从收获到罐装间隔不到4小时
Dialogue: 1,0:17:22.44,0:17:26.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Less than 4 hours pass between harvesting and canning procedures,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.52,0:17:30.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,以尽可能保留成品的营养价值
Dialogue: 1,0:17:26.52,0:17:30.12,Original,,0,0,0,,so as to conserve much of the nutritional value of the product to be sold.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.32,0:17:35.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,卸下卡车上的玉米就开始了整个流程
Dialogue: 1,0:17:33.32,0:17:35.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The unloading of the trucks starts the process
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.04,0:17:41.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里每年要罐装13.6万吨玉米
Dialogue: 1,0:17:36.04,0:17:41.32,Original,,0,0,0,,that annually consumes the 136,000 tons of corn that is canned here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.36,0:17:47.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,玉米棒通过传送带运入工厂
Dialogue: 1,0:17:44.36,0:17:47.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The cobs are transported into the plant on a conveyor,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.88,0:17:50.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,首先经过去粒机
Dialogue: 1,0:17:47.88,0:17:50.20,Original,,0,0,0,,and will first pass through a kernel remover.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.48,0:17:56.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台设备装有多个反向旋转的滚筒
Dialogue: 1,0:17:53.48,0:17:56.60,Original,,0,0,0,,A unit equipped with several counter-rotating cylinders,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.16,0:18:00.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,去除包裹着玉米棒叶子和须
Dialogue: 1,0:17:57.16,0:18:00.12,Original,,0,0,0,,removes the leaves and silk which surround the cob.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.84,0:18:05.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,短短几秒内，玉米棒外层就被完全剥离
Dialogue: 1,0:18:00.84,0:18:05.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Within only a few seconds, the cob is completely stripped of its covering.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.48,0:18:16.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,在这里排好队，等待去粒机处理
Dialogue: 1,0:18:13.48,0:18:16.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Here they are lined up, ready to be handled by the kernel remover.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.28,0:18:25.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,玉米棒穿过机器时被脱粒
Dialogue: 1,0:18:22.28,0:18:25.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The kernels are removed from the cobs by going through the machine,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.20,0:18:29.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,刀片在眨眼间切下玉米粒
Dialogue: 1,0:18:26.20,0:18:29.16,Original,,0,0,0,,where knives remove the kernels in a fraction of a second.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.88,0:18:34.74,Translation,,0,0,0,,每台设备每小时能对1.5吨玉米脱粒处理
Dialogue: 1,0:18:29.88,0:18:34.74,Original,,0,0,0,,Each of these units remove 1.5 tons of kernels every hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.28,0:18:39.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,每天停机2次，检查、清洁并磨快刀片
Dialogue: 1,0:18:35.28,0:18:39.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Twice a day, the machines are stopped to inspect, clean and sharpen the blades.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.62,0:18:44.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,玉米粒落向中间
Dialogue: 1,0:18:42.62,0:18:44.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The corn kernels fall into the middle,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.28,0:18:47.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,玉米棒从旁边丢下
Dialogue: 1,0:18:45.28,0:18:47.84,Original,,0,0,0,,while the cobs themselves are moved to the sides.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.12,0:18:57.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,玉米粒进入这台旋转滚筒
Dialogue: 1,0:18:55.12,0:18:57.84,Original,,0,0,0,,The kernels are entered into this rotating drum,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.32,0:19:00.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,去除比玉米粒大的杂质
Dialogue: 1,0:18:58.32,0:19:00.96,Original,,0,0,0,,which removes any particles larger than the kernels.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.32,0:19:04.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,这一过程中没有任何浪费
Dialogue: 1,0:19:02.32,0:19:04.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Nothing is wasted in this processing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.64,0:19:09.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,玉米渣、叶子和玉米棒之后用作动物饲料
Dialogue: 1,0:19:04.64,0:19:09.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Corn residues, leaves, and cobs will be used later as animal feed.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.88,0:19:17.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,玉米粒落入由水和切粒时榨出的玉米汁组成的混合液
Dialogue: 1,0:19:10.88,0:19:17.12,Original,,0,0,0,,Now, the kernels fall into a mix composed of water and the juice obtained when cutting the corn kernels themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.28,0:19:25.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,这种液体混合液可以输送玉米粒而不损伤它们
Dialogue: 1,0:19:21.28,0:19:25.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The liquid mix allows for the transporting of the kernels without damaging them.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.24,0:19:40.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,烫漂在这台巨大的滚筒中进行
Dialogue: 1,0:19:38.24,0:19:40.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Blanching is carried out in this huge cylinder.
Dialogue: 2,0:19:38.24,0:19:41.74,Annotation,,0,0,0,,烫漂：热水短时加热以灭酶护色
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.92,0:19:44.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,螺旋输送器把烫漂过的玉米粒送到表面
Dialogue: 1,0:19:41.92,0:19:44.80,Original,,0,0,0,,A worm screw brings the blanched kernels to the surface,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.44,0:19:48.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,在这里进行目视检查，检验玉米粒的质量
Dialogue: 1,0:19:45.44,0:19:48.16,Original,,0,0,0,,where a visual inspection verifies the quality of the kernels.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.38,0:19:56.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,剩下的就是装入罐头
Dialogue: 1,0:19:53.38,0:19:56.40,Original,,0,0,0,,All that remains is to pack them into these cans.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.66,0:20:01.22,Translation,,0,0,0,,成千上万的罐头被送往装罐车间
Dialogue: 1,0:19:58.66,0:20:01.22,Original,,0,0,0,,Thousands of cans are carried to the filling department.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.74,0:20:07.86,Translation,,0,0,0,,装罐由这台旋转式灌装机完成
Dialogue: 1,0:20:04.74,0:20:07.86,Original,,0,0,0,,Filling the cans is done from this rotating filling machine,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.50,0:20:11.94,Translation,,0,0,0,,每分钟最多可灌装450罐
Dialogue: 1,0:20:08.50,0:20:11.94,Original,,0,0,0,,and can handle up to 450 cans a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.50,0:20:20.58,Translation,,0,0,0,,落到一旁的玉米粒
Dialogue: 1,0:20:18.50,0:20:20.58,Original,,0,0,0,,The kernels, which fall to the side,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.82,0:20:23.30,Translation,,0,0,0,,稍后会被收集起来，送回灌装线
Dialogue: 1,0:20:20.82,0:20:23.30,Original,,0,0,0,,are gathered up later and returned to the filling line.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.42,0:20:28.98,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里加入由水、盐和糖配成的盐水
Dialogue: 1,0:20:24.42,0:20:28.98,Original,,0,0,0,,Here, a brine composed of water, salt, and sugar is added.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.74,0:20:35.22,Translation,,0,0,0,,盖子被牢牢盖在罐子上
Dialogue: 1,0:20:32.74,0:20:35.22,Original,,0,0,0,,Lids are securely attached onto the containers.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.50,0:20:38.42,Translation,,0,0,0,,但罐装还没结束
Dialogue: 1,0:20:36.50,0:20:38.42,Original,,0,0,0,,But the canning is not yet finished,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.90,0:20:40.98,Translation,,0,0,0,,因为重要的质检还没开始
Dialogue: 1,0:20:38.90,0:20:40.98,Original,,0,0,0,,as important tests have to be carried out.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.34,0:20:49.06,Translation,,0,0,0,,实验室检测确保产品质量
Dialogue: 1,0:20:46.34,0:20:49.06,Original,,0,0,0,,Laboratory tests assure the quality of the product.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.58,0:20:53.30,Translation,,0,0,0,,首先检测罐头的密封性
Dialogue: 1,0:20:50.58,0:20:53.30,Original,,0,0,0,,First, the watertight properties of the cans,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.78,0:20:56.82,Translation,,0,0,0,,再检查灌装重量和玉米粒品质
Dialogue: 1,0:20:53.78,0:20:56.82,Original,,0,0,0,,then the filling weight, and the quality of the kernels are checked.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.94,0:21:02.90,Translation,,0,0,0,,与此同时，罐头继续在工厂中行进
Dialogue: 1,0:20:59.94,0:21:02.90,Original,,0,0,0,,In the meantime, cans continue their way through the plant,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.90,0:21:06.18,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有最后一步：杀菌
Dialogue: 1,0:21:02.90,0:21:06.18,Original,,0,0,0,,and one step remains: sterilisation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.30,0:21:14.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,杀菌在这台炉子中进行，温度120摄氏度，最长持续6分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:21:07.30,0:21:14.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Sterilisation takes place in this oven at 120 degrees centigrade and lasts up to 6 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.52,0:21:23.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,这是关键一步，确保产品保质期长达18个月
Dialogue: 1,0:21:16.52,0:21:23.40,Original,,0,0,0,,This is a crucial step, because it guarantees that the product is reliable and that it will remain so for 18 months.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.44,0:21:30.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后进行口味抽样，确认甜玉米符合质量标准
Dialogue: 1,0:21:24.44,0:21:30.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Lastly, taste samples are carried out to determine that the sweet corn hits quality standards.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.40,0:21:33.06,Translation,,0,0,0,,在这座庞大的工厂里
Dialogue: 1,0:21:31.40,0:21:33.06,Original,,0,0,0,,In this giant facility
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.06,0:21:38.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,每年能生产出惊人的4300万罐玉米
Dialogue: 1,0:21:33.06,0:21:38.28,Original,,0,0,0,,an amazing total of 43 million cans of corn are produced every year.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.16,0:21:42.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,一个囊中羞涩学生的美食梦想
Dialogue: 1,0:21:39.16,0:21:42.00,Original,,0,0,0,,A cash-strapped student's culinary dream.
